},{"id":"A5079746376","name":"Michael C. Double"},{"id":"A5024862277","name":"Marco Favero"},{"id":"A5042394854","name":"Flavio Quintana"},{"id":"A5112867207","name":"Mark L. Tasker"},{"id":"A5002019741","name":"Henri Weimerskirch"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"},{"id":"A5025973700","name":"Anton C. Wolfaardt"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":263,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biocon.2016.06.017","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I1294671590","I1319328641","I1330876588","I141816643","I151201029","I2801630795","I4210095510","I4210135039","I4394709165","I4405256283","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Biological Conservation","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"bronze","oa_url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0006320716302427","openalex_topics":["T10089","T10659","T11913"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10089","pub_date":"2016-07-15","study_type":"article","title":"The conservation status and priorities for albatrosses and large petrels","type":"article","work_id":"W2483513376","year":2016},{"abstract":"","author_count":6,"author_ids":["A5013386732","A5027857455","A5057408039","A5065509561","A5090932784"],"author_institution_ids":["I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5090932784","name":"Luc\u00eda Alzugaray"},{"id":"","name":"M. Di Martino"},{"id":"A5013386732","name":"Lucas E. Beltramino"},{"id":"A5057408039","name":"Victoria J. Rowntree"},{"id":"A5027857455","name":"Mariano Sironi"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":19,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpolbul.2020.111738","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I166401450","I223532165","I4405262879","I84218800"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","last_updated":"2026-11-07T11:25:07.637180","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpolbul.2020.111738","openalex_topics":["T10659","T10753","T11656"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2020-10-13","study_type":"article","title":"Anthropogenic debris in the digestive tract of a southern right whale (Eubalaena australis) stranded in Golfo Nuevo, Argentina","type":"article","work_id":"W3093335786","year":2020},{"abstract":"","author_count":6,"author_ids":["A5014427421","A5048284589","A5065509561","A5075732279","A5075765975","A5086477070"],"author_institution_ids":["I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5086477070","name":"Ralph Eric Thijl Vanstreels"},{"id":"A5075765975","name":"Luciana Gallo"},{"id":"A5075732279","name":"Patr\u00edcia Pereira Serafini"},{"id":"A5014427421","name":"Allan Poltronieri Santos"},{"id":"A5048284589","name":"Leandro Egert"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":22,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpolbul.2021.113046","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk"],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I151201029","I4210139426","I4405256283","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","last_updated":"2026-11-04T10:54:05.112534","license":"cc-by-nc-sa","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"http://hdl.handle.net/11336/167102","openalex_topics":["T10659","T10753","T11656"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2021-10-19","study_type":"article","title":"Ingestion of plastics and other debris by coastal and pelagic birds along the coast of Esp\u00edrito Santo, Eastern Brazil","type":"article","work_id":"W3205598821","year":2021},{"abstract":"Plastic ingestion is a problem for seabirds worldwide. In addition to direct health effects such as obstruction or perforation of the gastrointestinal tract, plastic ingestion can also lead to indirect health effects through the release of chemicals that may be absorbed and cause systemic and chronic toxicity. Among chemicals that can be released by plastics are phthalate esters, a group of chemicals widely used as plasticizers or additives to change the physical characteristics of plastics. In this study, three phthalate esters, dimethyl phthalate (DMP), dibuthyl phthalate (DBP), and diethylhexyl phthalate (DEHP), were quantified in the uropygial gland of 48 seabirds from 16 species collected ashore in a tropical region, the coast of Esp\u00edrito Santo, Eastern Brazil. Including trace levels, DMP was detected in 16 birds (33%) from 10 species, with an average concentration of 0.014 \u00b1 0.005 ng/\u00b5l (mean \u00b1 SD for individuals with concentrations above the practical level of detection of 0.01 ng/\u00b5l). DBP was detected in 15 birds (31%) from 11 species, with an average concentration of 0.049 \u00b1 0.032 ng/\u00b5l. DEHP was detected in 21 birds (44%) from 11 species, with an average concentration of 0.115 \u00b1 0.105 ng/\u00b5l. DMP concentration in the uropygial gland was positively associated with the presence, number, and mass of plastic items in the upper digestive tract. However, no such relationship was noted for DBP nor DEHP, suggesting the concentration of phthalate compounds in the uropygial gland might not always serve as a reliable proxy for plastic ingestion. In spite of relatively high frequencies of detection, the low concentrations of phthalates detected in this study suggest levels of exposure below known toxicity thresholds. Further studies on the potential adverse effects of phthalate exposure in seabirds are necessary, especially on the reproductive development of embryos and chicks.","author_count":9,"author_ids":["A5014427421","A5048284589","A5053051965","A5065509561","A5075732279","A5075765975","A5077074620","A5086477070"],"author_institution_ids":["I151201029","I4104125","I4210139426","I4210163949","I4405256283","I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5086477070","name":"Ralph Eric Thijl Vanstreels"},{"id":"A5077074620","name":"Isadora N. Piccinin"},{"id":"A5053051965","name":"Marcelo Maraschin"},{"id":"A5075765975","name":"Luciana Gallo"},{"id":"A5075732279","name":"Patr\u00edcia Pereira Serafini"},{"id":"","name":"Alice Pereira"},{"id":"A5014427421","name":"Allan Poltronieri Santos"},{"id":"A5048284589","name":"Leandro Egert"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":18,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1638/2022-0053","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk","risk_assessment"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I151201029","I4104125","I4210139426","I4210163949","I4405256283","I84218800"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Journal of Zoo and Wildlife Medicine","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1638/2022-0053","openalex_topics":["T10447","T10686","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2023-01-05","study_type":"article","title":"PHTHALATE ESTERS (PLASTICIZERS) IN THE UROPYGIAL GLAND AND THEIR RELATIONSHIP TO PLASTICS INGESTION IN SEABIRDS ALONG THE COAST OF ESP\u00cdRITO SANTO, EASTERN BRAZIL","type":"article","work_id":"W4313703396","year":2023},{"abstract":"","author_count":17,"author_ids":["A5021055138","A5027124830","A5053051965","A5062279092","A5065509561","A5065647151","A5075732279","A5075765975","A5077074620","A5080994163","A5081798077","A5081889580","A5083804866","A5084426469","A5084695324","A5086477070"],"author_institution_ids":["I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5075732279","name":"Patr\u00edcia Pereira Serafini"},{"id":"A5080994163","name":"B Righetti"},{"id":"A5086477070","name":"Ralph Eric Thijl Vanstreels"},{"id":"A5021055138","name":"Leandro Bugoni"},{"id":"A5065647151","name":"Clei Endrigo Piazza"},{"id":"A5084695324","name":"Da\u00edna Lima"},{"id":"A5081798077","name":"Jac\u00f3 Joaquim Mattos"},{"id":"A5083804866","name":"Cristiane K. M. Kolesnikovas"},{"id":"","name":"Alice Pereira"},{"id":"A5053051965","name":"Marcelo Maraschin"},{"id":"A5077074620","name":"Isadora N. Piccinin"},{"id":"A5062279092","name":"Tim Guilford"},{"id":"A5075765975","name":"Luciana Gallo"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"},{"id":"A5084426469","name":"Rafael Andr\u00e9 Louren\u00e7o"},{"id":"A5027124830","name":"Afonso Celso Dias Bainy"},{"id":"A5081889580","name":"Karim H. L\u00fcchmann"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":10,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpolbul.2024.116398","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I126460647","I151201029","I164790352","I17974374","I40120149","I4104125","I4210139426","I4210149661","I4210163949","I4405256283","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","last_updated":"2026-11-11T12:16:26.678958","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://ora.ox.ac.uk/objects/uuid:a751da28-32e8-4ace-8a26-185d81a29385/files/rqf85nc33v","openalex_topics":["T10122","T10447","T10753"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10447","pub_date":"2024-05-08","study_type":"article","title":"Biochemical and molecular biomarkers and their association with anthropogenic chemicals in wintering Manx shearwaters (Puffinus puffinus)","type":"article","work_id":"W4396758916","year":2024},{"abstract":"","author_count":16,"author_ids":["A5006318013","A5018898998","A5037746239","A5045541121","A5065509561","A5066926337","A5075700355","A5075732279","A5075765975","A5083804866","A5086477070","A5088445157","A5103262467","A5111153117","A5112872457"],"author_institution_ids":["I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5075765975","name":"Luciana Gallo"},{"id":"A5075732279","name":"Patr\u00edcia Pereira Serafini"},{"id":"A5086477070","name":"Ralph Eric Thijl Vanstreels"},{"id":"A5103262467","name":"Leandro Luis Tamini"},{"id":"A5083804866","name":"Cristiane K. M. Kolesnikovas"},{"id":"","name":"Alice Pereira"},{"id":"A5111153117","name":"Tatiana S. Neves"},{"id":"A5075700355","name":"Gabriel David do Nascimento"},{"id":"A5066926337","name":"Lucas S. Rodr\u00edguez Pirani"},{"id":"A5045541121","name":"A. Lorena Picone"},{"id":"A5018898998","name":"Rosana M. Romano"},{"id":"A5112872457","name":"C. Karina Alvarez"},{"id":"A5006318013","name":"Sergio Andres Rodr\u00edguez Heredia"},{"id":"A5088445157","name":"Leandro Nahuel Chavez"},{"id":"A5037746239","name":"Rub\u00e9n F. Dellacasa"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":7,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpolbul.2024.117094","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk","occurrence_and_monitoring"],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I151201029","I2799719156","I4104125","I4210139426","I4210149661","I4210163949","I4405256283","I84218800","I874386039"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Marine Pollution Bulletin","last_updated":"2026-11-09T13:22:03.289127","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4775131","openalex_topics":["T10659","T10753","T11656"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2024-11-01","study_type":"article","title":"High frequency of plastic ingestion in procellariiform seabirds (albatrosses, petrels and shearwaters) in the Southwest Atlantic Ocean","type":"article","work_id":"W4403985685","year":2024},{"abstract":"Abstract Phthalate acid esters (PAEs) are widely used plastic additives that have become ubiquitous contaminants in marine environments. Filter-feeding baleen whales may be exposed to these pollutants through water, prey or ingested plastic debris. While macroplastics have been reported in the gut of a southern right whale (SRW, Eubalaena australis ), exposure to PAEs has not been assessed. Here, we quantified three lipophilic PAEs, dimethyl phthalate (DMP), dibutyl phthalate (DBP), and di-2-ethylhexyl phthalate (DEHP), in the blubber of 13 SRWs (three calves, three juveniles and seven adults) stranded in 2021 at Pen\u00ednsula Vald\u00e9s, Argentina. More than 90% of samples contained detectable PAE levels, and 46.2% were above quantification limits. DEHP and DBP were the most prevalent compounds (61.5% and 30.8%, respectively), although the biological significance of the detected concentrations remains uncertain. This is the first report of PAEs in SRW blubber and suggests potential mother-calf transfer, highlighting exposure of Southern Hemisphere mysticetes to plastic-derived chemicals.","author_count":7,"author_ids":["A5001221857","A5027857455","A5065509561","A5070784016","A5075765975","A5101270603","A5104263399"],"author_institution_ids":["I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5075765975","name":"Luciana Gallo"},{"id":"A5001221857","name":"Melina P. Michlig"},{"id":"A5070784016","name":"Mar\u00eda Rosa Repetti"},{"id":"A5104263399","name":"Agustina Donini"},{"id":"A5101270603","name":"Adri\u00e1n E. Rodr\u00edguez"},{"id":"A5027857455","name":"Mariano Sironi"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00300-026-03508-8","domain_tags":["analytical_methods"],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I151201029","I166401450","I3121987637","I4210163949","I4405256283","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Polar Biology","last_updated":"2026-10-14T16:39:01.820549","license":"cc-by","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"hybrid","oa_url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s00300-026-03508-8.pdf","openalex_topics":["T10659","T10686","T10753"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10686","pub_date":"2026-06-26","study_type":"article","title":"First report of phthalate acid esters (plasticizers) in blubber of southern right whales (Eubalaena australis) from Pen\u00ednsula Vald\u00e9s, Argentina","type":"article","work_id":"W7166045178","year":2026},{"abstract":"The sub-lethal effects of plastics and their associated chemicals on wildlife are poorly understood, primarily due to the lack of reliable indicators. We used southern giant petrels (Macronectes giganteus, SGP), key scavengers and predators in southern seas, to assess whether early-life exposure to plastics was associated with health parameters. We examined relationships between plastic ingestion (\u2265 1 mm) and biomarkers of enzymatic activities (AChE acetylcholinesterase, BChE butyrylcholinesterase and GST glutathione S-transferase) and conventional health parameters (haematological, biochemical and morphometric data) in SGP chicks from colonies in Chubut, Argentina. During 2022 and 2023, plastics were detected in 71.4% of chicks (1-14 items, mean mass = 0.2510 g, representing < 0.1% of chick body mass). In 30-day-old chicks, plastic ingestion was associated with nutritional parameters (cholesterol, total solids, packed cell volume, calcium, body mass and body condition index), metabolism (enzymes aspartate aminotransferase, alkaline phosphatase, lactate dehydrogenase, creatinine phosphokinase) and immune response (eosinophil percentage). Associations with biomarkers (AChE, BChE, and GST) were observed but lost significance when accounting for inter-annual variation. By fledging (\u223c90 days), most relationships weakened or disappeared, while GST activity and calcium levels emerged as the only variables associated with plastic ingestion. It is unclear whether these associations reflect compensatory physiological responses to oxidative challenge, contaminant exposure, or developmental/ontogenetic adjustments. Our results highlight the value of multi-indicator approaches for detecting subtle physiological variation associated with plastic ingestion. Importantly, the pervasive threat of plastic pollution warrants investigating whether early-life exposure influences post-fledging survival and fitness.","author_count":4,"author_ids":["A5042394854","A5045673160","A5065509561","A5075765975"],"author_institution_ids":["I84218800"],"authors":[{"id":"A5075765975","name":"Luciana Gallo"},{"id":"A5042394854","name":"Flavio Quintana"},{"id":"A5045673160","name":"Andr\u00e9s Maximiliano Attademo"},{"id":"A5065509561","name":"Marcela Uhart"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoenv.2026.120628","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I151201029","I3121987637","I4210163949","I4405256283","I84218800"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Ecotoxicology and Environmental Safety","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"cc-by","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"gold","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoenv.2026.120628","openalex_topics":["T10447","T10753","T11656"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2026-08-11","study_type":"article","title":"Early-life exposure to plastics is associated with health parameters and biomarkers in southern giant petrels","type":"article","work_id":"W7202158458","year":2026}]}
